message: "If you use this software or cite its computational models, please cite it as below."
title: "PowerLab: Deterministic Energy Systems & Battery Storage Calculation Suite"
authors:
  - family-names: "Saadidi"
    given-names: "Miad"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-4501-7590"
url: "https://powelab.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/miadsaadidi/powerlab"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-05"
license: "MIT"
abstract: "PowerLab is an open-source deterministic computational modeling platform designed to unify clean energy planning across solar photovoltaics, battery storage systems, residential electrical loads, and electric vehicles. The platform implements pure mathematical formulations adhering to IEEE Std 485, National Electrical Code (NEC/NFPA 70), and NREL PVWatts V8 algorithms with zero database tracking."
keywords:
  - "solar-pv"
  - "photovoltaics"
  - "battery-storage"
  - "energy-storage"
  - "peukert-effect"
  - "inverter-efficiency"
  - "load-sizing"
  - "electric-vehicles"
  - "clean-energy"
  - "engineering-calculators"
